title: kanban-md round trip drops karr's foundation config, silently re-enabling a
  disabled board
updated: 2026-08-10T03:48:51Z
---

Found by the #60 fix, verified against a kanban-md binary built from ../kanban-md.

Loading a karr-materialized view with kanban-md rewrites config.yml on the spot:
it migrates version 1 to version 10 and re-saves the file. karr's `foundation`
key is not in the Go schema, so it does not survive that round trip.

Consequence: a board turned off with `karr disable` is silently turned back on.
The sequence is ordinary interop usage, not an edge case:

    karr disable            # foundation.enabled = 0 in refs/karr/config
    karr materialize        # view carries foundation: enabled: 0
    kanban list             # kanban-md migrates and re-saves config.yml
    karr import --yes       # foundation key is gone -> defaults -> enabled

karr-foundation then starts running agents on a board the maintainer switched
off. Nothing warns at any step.

Pre-existing, but only reachable since #60 made the view loadable by kanban-md
at all. Related: #82 in the sense that both are "the other side was empty for
the wrong reason".

Options, none obviously right:
- import preserves keys the file view cannot represent, by diffing against the
  ref config rather than replacing it (also fixes the sibling ticket about
  config pollution)
- materialize writes karr-only keys somewhere kanban-md will not touch
- import refuses when the view's config lost keys the board had, and says so

Whichever way, `karr disable` must not be undoable by a tool that never heard
of it.
Geschlossen durch bc3b87e/306180d: import reconciled die View gegen refs/karr/config statt sie zu ersetzen; foundation/lock_timeout ueberleben den kanban-md-Roundtrip. Verifiziert gegen kanban-md-Binary, t/102.
